001b[85Gaway\u001b[90Gtoo.\r\u001b[8C\u001b[1Bplann\u001b[15Gd mesh-shader \u001b[30Gath (J40) and ray-traced hit shading (J47) become\u001b[80Gmuch\u001b[85Geasier. Per-material\u001b[106Gdescriptor\u001b[117Gsets\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gar\u001b[9Gawkwar\u001b[17Gfor both, and ray-traced hit shading effectively needs bindless.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BThe\u001b[7Gcost\u001b[12Gis\u001b[15Ga\u001b[17Gbigger\u001b[24Gchange.\u001b[32GShaders\u001b[40Ghave\u001b[45Gto\u001b[48Gmark\u001b[53Gtexture\u001b[61Gindices\u001b[69Gwith\u001b[74G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mnonuniformEXT\u001b[88G\u001b[39mwhere\u001b[94Gthey\u001b[99Gvary\u001b[104Gacross\u001b[111Ga\u001b[113Gdraw.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BStand-ins become fixed i\u001b[28Gdices in the \u001b[42Grray,\u001b[76Go read. J64\u001b[88Galready moves vertex data to\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
