[0.118, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Message\u001b[14Gqueued\u001b[21Gfor delivery to\u001b[37Ga006364b5939cc9f5 at its next\u001b[68Gool\u001b[77G. Sending this moved nothing it\u001b[109Gis\u001b[112G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mru\u001b[9Gning to the background just now, so\u001b[45Gthe mess\u001b[54Gge\u001b[57Gwaits for that round unless\u001b[85Gsomething moves sooner. If it \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bfinishes first, it is resumed with the message and notifies again, so wait for that notification before \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bresending.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI've sav\u001b[12Gd the n\u001b[20Gw workf\u001b[29Gw as \u001b[35G memory and told both implementers there's no full gate in the\u001b[98Glanes. My J63 build\u001b[118Gis\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bqueued\u001b[10Gbehind\u001b[17Gthe\u001b[21Gheavy\u001b[27Glock\u001b[32Gthat\u001b[37Gthe\u001b[41GL15a\u001b[46Ggate\u001b[51Gholds,\u001b[58Gand\u001b[62Gthe\u001b[66Gcurrent\u001b[74Gbatch\u001b[80Gis\u001b[83GJ63,\u001b[88GJ36,\u001b[93GL15a\u001b[98Gand\u001b[102GW22b.\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · summary\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mClang-tidy only needs to be run with the full gate, it often is just correctly small style issues. The same with the \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mwhitespace linefeed script. A good working build of the software and local check that it is complete and working is \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255menough to considered ready to merge. We will deal with issues at merge time as a batch.\u001b[39m                               \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m \u001b[39m Reading \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file, running \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command…\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ sed -n 1,40p '/home/ivan/projects/jettison.lane-b/'docs/history.md\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[5B\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[20;3H\u001b[?25h"]
