[0.171, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[14BEdit\u001b[11G~/projects/jettison.lane-c/docs/decisions.md\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mUpdate(~/projects/jettison.lane-c/docs/decisions.md)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✻\u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;218;124;92mBooping…\u001b[71G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m2\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.076, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 226 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **A game's content mounts under its own identifier** (2026-11-27, the user's). The shell mounts a   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 227 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  game's content under its `mod.yaml`'s `identifier`, `base` when it has none, so a mod's             \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 228 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  `requires` can name it (`manifest`) and a dedicated server's session, which names it the same,      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 229 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  agrees with the client on the world content's packages. Overlays requiring `base` instead was       \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 230 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  rejected. [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mFiles, packs and mods\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](files-and-mods.md#the-shells-mounts)                              \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 231 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m-\u001b[14G**Pack\u001b[21Gfiles\u001b[27Gare\u001b[31Gcompressed\u001b[42Gwith\u001b[47Gzstd,\u001b[53Gone\u001b[57Gcopy\u001b[62Gshared\u001b[69Gwith\u001b[74Glibktx**\u001b[83G(2026-11-13).\u001b[97Glibktx\u001b[104Gcompiles\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 232 \u001b[22m   its own zstd with pu\u001b[35Glic symbols and\u001b[51Gno\u001b[54Goption\u001b[61Gfor\u001b[65Ganother,\u001b[74Gso\u001b[77Gthe\u001b[81Gengine\u001b[88Gbuilds\u001b[95Gzstd\u001b[100G1.5.7\u001b[106Gonce\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 233 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m \u001b[14Gand builds `ktx_read`\u001b[36Gagainst\u001b[44Git,\u001b[48Gtaking\u001b[55Glibktx's\u001b[64Gcopy\u001b[69Gout\u001b[73Gof\u001b[76Gits\u001b[80Gsources\u001b[88Gin\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;107;128m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/projects/jettison.lane-c/docs/history.md)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[38;2;255;107;128mError: Found 2 matches of the string to replace, but replace_all is false. To replace all occurrences, set \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;107;128mreplace_all to true. To replace only one occurrence, please provide more context to uniquely identify the instance.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BString: | --- | --- |\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[38;2;255;107;128mError: edit /home/ivan/projects/jettison.lane-c/docs/history.md: Found 2 matches of the string to replace, and an \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;255;107;128medit must match exactly once. Pass {all: true} to replace every match, or give more surrounding text so the match \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;255;107;128mis unique.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[12C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m34\u001b[16G 28s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m49.2k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[20C\u001b[6B\u001b[38;2;0;204;204m2\r\u001b[98C\u001b[3B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m4\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.060, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[47C\u001b[22B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[2m2\u001b[50G6\u001b[54G939\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
