[0.037, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[2m 223 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 224 \u001b[22m ## Files, packs and mods\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 225 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[8C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m6\u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m-\u001b[14G**A game's content mounts\u001b[40Gunder its\u001b[50Gow\u001b[53G identifier** (2026-11-27, the user's). The shell mounts\u001b[110Ga\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m27\u001b[14G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mgam\u001b[18G's content under its `mod.yaml`'s `identifier`, `base` when it has none, so a mod's             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 228 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  `requires` can name it (`manifest`) and a dedicated server's session, which names it the same,      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 229 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  agrees with the client on the world content's packages. Overlays requiring `base` instead was       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 230 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  rejected. [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mFiles, packs and mods\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](files-and-mods.md#the-shells-mounts)                              \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 231 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m-\u001b[14G**Pack\u001b[21Gfiles\u001b[27Gare\u001b[31Gcompressed\u001b[42Gwith\u001b[47Gzstd,\u001b[53Gone\u001b[57Gcopy\u001b[62Gshared\u001b[69Gwith\u001b[74Glibktx**\u001b[83G(2026-11-13).\u001b[97Glibktx\u001b[104Gcompiles\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 232 \u001b[22m   its own zs\u001b[25Gd with public symbols and no\u001b[54Goption\u001b[61Gfor\u001b[65Ganother,\u001b[74Gso\u001b[77Gthe\u001b[81Gengine\u001b[88Gbuilds\u001b[95Gzstd\u001b[100G1.5.7\u001b[106Gonce\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 233 \u001b[22m   and builds `ktx_read` against it, taking libktx's copy out of its sources in\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;107;128m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/projects/jet